          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Urological Supplies Helpful Information",
            "text": "<p><strong>What are Urological Supplies</strong><br/><br/>Urological supplies are products used to support and manage urinary tract health and related conditions. These supplies are essential for individuals with urinary incontinence, difficulty urinating, or other urological issues. </p><p><strong>Types of Urological Supplies</strong></p><p>Key types of urological supplies include:<br/><br/><strong>Catheters:</strong></p><p><strong>Intermittent Catheters:</strong> Used temporarily to drain urine from the bladder.<br/><strong>Indwelling Foley Catheters:</strong> Inserted into the bladder for continuous drainage.<br/><strong>External Catheters:</strong> Worn externally, typically for males (e.g., condom catheters).</p><p><strong>Drainage Bags:</strong></p><p><strong>Leg Bags</strong>: Worn on the leg for mobility and to collect urine.<br/><strong>Urinary Drainage Bags:</strong> Larger capacity bags used overnight.</p><p><strong>Catheter Insertion Kits: </strong>Include necessary items for sterile catheter insertion, like gloves, lubricant, and antiseptic wipes.</p><p><strong>Penile Sheaths: </strong>Used to manage incontinence in men without the need for a catheter.</p><p><strong>Incontinence Pads and Briefs: </strong>Absorbent products designed to manage urinary leakage.</p><p><strong>Cystoscopy Supplies: </strong>Instruments and tools for examining the bladder.</p><p><strong>Urinary Drainage Accessories: </strong>Tubing, clamps, and connectors to aid in the management of urinary drainage systems.</p><p>These supplies are crucial for maintaining hygiene, comfort, and quality of life for individuals with urological needs.</p>",
            "heading_size": "medium",
            "text_alignment": "left"
          }
        }
      },
